      "claim": "Record C03 directly demonstrates that ACT001, the dimethylamino-Michael adduct of parthenolide whose scaffold and dimethylamino-lactone pharmacophore match the query, achieves brain concentrations exceeding plasma in rats after oral administration (12,749 vs 6,971 ng/mL), providing strong evidence of meaningful CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is structurally the ACT001/DMAMCL-type dimethylamino lactone, and the closest experimental record shows ACT001 penetrates the BBB with brain concentrations higher than plasma in rats. This direct evidence outweighs lower-similarity steroid negatives, supporting a pass for meaningful CNS access.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct Kp,uu or unbound brain-to-plasma ratio is available for the query; the ACT001 evidence is based on total brain tissue concentration.",
    "Species and route differences (rat oral vs potential clinical use) are not fully addressed.",
    "Efflux transporter status for the query was not explicitly measured, though the tertiary amine may engage uptake transporters."
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [],
  "revision_action": "initial"
}

